[2026-05-31 12:14] Task 3 shipped at 240288c. Dispatch — **CHORE-75 Task 4 RED: MvoxNav wires AvatarMenu**.

Plan ref: Task 4 Steps 1-2.

Per plan:
1. Read existing `src/lib/components/MvoxNav.spec.ts`. Add a new test asserting MvoxNav renders the AvatarMenu trigger when signedIn=true:
   ```ts
   it('renders AvatarMenu trigger when signedIn (CHORE-75)', () => {
     const { container } = render(MvoxNav, {
       signedIn: true,
       userName: 'Mihkel Putrinš',
       userInitial: 'M',
       currentTab: 'agenda',
     });
     const trigger = container.querySelector('button[data-testid="avatar-menu-trigger"]');
     expect(trigger).not.toBeNull();
     expect(trigger?.textContent).toContain('M');
   });
   ```

2. If existing MvoxNav tests assert the inline-avatar text shape (the `<span>{userName}</span>` next to a tile), update those assertions to expect the new AvatarMenu trigger shape. Invoke the **Bentham CHORE-72-Task-15 mechanical-update rule** + flag in your handoff message AND in the eventual commit body. Spec intent (signed-in user sees their name) is preserved — name now lives in the dropdown panel.

